    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Speech-to-Text**\n\nI've decided to move forward with Google Cloud Speech-to-Text. It seems like a robust choice for handling the audio streaming and interim transcript requirement. The `google-cloud-speech` library will be a key dependency in implementing the microphone stream.\n\n\n**Defining Implementation Steps**\n\nI'm now outlining the implementation steps. My current focus is creating the `stream_microphone.py` file. I'll need to import relevant libraries like `speech_v1p1beta1`, `pyaudio`, and `queue`. Then I will set up PyAudio for microphone input and create a `buffer_generator` to feed audio to the Google Cloud Speech-to-Text API. Finally I will configure the `streaming_recognition_config` and process API responses.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789864958213,
          "start": 1789864953220
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc43c584001uWers41Diyy9c0",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc43bedc001d3r0iDZO3Q0OUa",
      "session_id": "ses_f43bc41a6ffeowEGPTXfIiGjUB",
